ls=[];cases=[];work=['# Data Center Foundations evidence workbook','','This workbook describes a classroom design and guided physical/vendor procedures. Browser calculations are not actual devices, electrical tests, cooling measurements or management sessions.','','## Three-rack baseline','','All racks have 42U, front-to-rear equipment airflow, front cold aisle and rear hot aisle. R1: storage U1–4, compute U5–12, leaf switches U40–41; 6 kW. R2: compute U1–12, leaf switches U40–41; 6 kW. R3: backup U1–4, leaves U36–37, spines U38–39, OOB switch U40; 4 kW. Blank unused front openings with supported panels. Rack dimensions, mass/rails, floor loading and approved inlet limits are separate installation checks.','','Every dual-cord device maps PSU A → rack PDU A → UPS A → supply domain A and PSU B → rack PDU B → UPS B → supply domain B. Each entire rack path has 10 kW rating with a declared planning allowance of 80%, hence 8 kW usable on either surviving path. Site total is 16 kW; each site supply/UPS path has a declared 25 kW rating and 80% allowance, hence 20 kW. These are invented design inputs, not universal derating rules or a licensed electrical plan. A/B labels alone do not establish upstream independence. Single-cord equipment needs a supported transfer/redundancy design and its own failure analysis.','','Cooling: declared 20 kW available sensible removal for 16 kW IT load. At 2 m³/s, assumed density 1.2 kg/m³ and specific heat 1.005 kJ/(kg·K), mean air rise is about 6.63 K. This does not establish maximum inlet, containment efficiency, humidity or cooling redundancy. Verify those with qualified facility staff and actual measurements.','','Fabric: two leaves per rack, two spines in R3; each leaf connects to both spines with 100 Gb/s links. The isolated worksheet compares a representative 48×25 Gb/s leaf (6:1 healthy, 12:1 with one uplink unavailable), not the smaller installed server population as a measured traffic demand. Show port/optic/speed/length and separate route A/B for each cable. Never infer single-flow 200 Gb/s from two uplinks.','','OOB: use documentation-only 192.0.2.0/24: jump host .10, controller inventory .21–.32, OOB switch .2; these are plan labels, not addresses configured on the host. Protected management ingress permits the named administrator read-only HTTPS operation to assigned controllers; guest/application clients are denied. DNS/time/logging and emergency console dependencies require explicit targets and scope. Keep BMC standby power and OOB switch/jump access independent of the workload path where supported; shared-NIC or shared-UPS coupling must be documented. No Internet exposure, default credentials or real secrets in the workbook.','','## Baseline/fault/restore record','','Record observer, timestamp, intended operation, attachment, supported versions and expected positive/negative observations. Save the exact owned baseline and independent recovery access. Introduce only one owned plan/configuration fault, retain its failure evidence, restore exact prior state, repeat original allowed and prohibited operations, then remove only owned artifacts. For physical work use approved qualified procedures; do not pull cables, open energized panels or force storage assembly on this host.','']
plan=runpy.run_path(str(R/'labs/data-center-plan.py'))['BASELINE'] if limit>=16 else None
if plan:
 work += ['## Endpoint cable and controller schedule','','Planned media and lengths below are invented inputs, requiring supported optics/channel/route verification. Routes A/B must be reviewed for actual physical diversity. The single R3 OOB switch and jump host remain named shared recovery dependencies; this plan does not claim fully redundant management. Server dual attachment requires a supported bonding/teaming and switch policy not deployed by this artifact. Storage/backup replication and storage-transport paths beyond the declared workload NICs are external scoped additions, never implicit permits.','','| Source | Destination | Planned media / length | Route |','| --- | --- | --- | --- |']
 work += ['| '+' | '.join(c)+' |' for c in plan['cables']]
 work += ['', 'Controller addresses .21–.32 follow the twelve named storage/compute/backup assets in the cable schedule. Switch management .40–.47 has separate role/target policy to design; the offline BMC read rule does not automatically authorize those switches. OOB switch .2 and jump .10 are plan labels only. DNS/time/logging, phase/outlet ratings, full rack mass/depth, cooling failure domains and emergency console remain explicit external checks.','']
